<p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> most white fuzz on young microgreens is harmless root hair. Real mold is a wet-and-still problem, and you fix it with air, not more chemistry. A $15 box fan ended months of mold for me after every spray failed. Check the <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=box+fan+for+plants&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">current price on a box fan</a>; most run $12 to $20. If you see one under $17, that is a solid deal and probably the last mold fix you will buy.</p>

